Each milestone ends in one video. The video is the reflection and the assessment: if Joel can explain a step to camera, he understands it.

The [print timelapses](/lore/timelapses) are separate: each one is a print plate sped up, linked from the milestone its parts belong to.

| Milestone | Video | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [M1. Bench it](/lore/m1-bench-it) | [M1 video](/lore/video-m1) | Planned |
| [M2. One joint end to end](/lore/m2-one-joint) | [M2 video](/lore/video-m2) | Planned |
| [M3. The whole arm moves](/lore/m3-whole-arm) | [M3 video](/lore/video-m3) | Planned |
| [M4. Pick and place](/lore/m4-pick-and-place) | [M4 video](/lore/video-m4) | Planned |
| [M5. Touch the skiff](/lore/m5-touch-the-skiff) | [M5 video](/lore/video-m5) | Planned |
| [M6. Patch a cable](/lore/m6-patch-a-cable) | [M6 video](/lore/video-m6) | Planned |
| [M7. Play it](/lore/m7-play-it) | [M7 video](/lore/video-m7) | Planned |

## Terms

- **milestone video**: the one published video that closes a milestone.
